<title>ITALY: Prodi says Italy has accounts in order for EMU.</title>
<headline>Prodi says Italy has accounts in order for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime minister Romano Prodi said on Thursday that Italy would go to next week's Amsterdam summit of EU leaders with its head high respecting key criteria for countries wishing to join European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>He said the only criterion that Italy currently failed to meet was the debt-gdp ratio but that this was being progressively worked on.</p>
</text>
